WEBVTT

00:11.011 --> 00:13.013
[rock music playing]

00:43.043 --> 00:46.714
CHAPTER 8: I'M SURE IT WAS MY GLASSES
YOU TROD ON EARLIER

00:46.797 --> 00:48.424
[metal gate opens, closes]

00:51.719 --> 00:54.054
EPISODE 3

00:57.141 --> 01:00.311
[sighs] Is he heading to the bus stop?

01:01.854 --> 01:04.899
Wait, does this mean
I'm going to run into him every morning?

01:07.276 --> 01:09.570
Shouldn't he be going to school
earlier than this?

01:20.956 --> 01:23.334
Geez, he's walking too slowly.

01:36.847 --> 01:37.973
What is he doing?

01:38.057 --> 01:40.184
-[screams]
-Huh?

01:40.267 --> 01:41.936
[shrieking]

01:44.563 --> 01:45.648
[grunts]

01:48.150 --> 01:49.151
What?

01:52.279 --> 01:53.447
Mr. Ga!

01:53.531 --> 01:55.574
Oh! Mr. Ga!

01:55.658 --> 01:56.826
[breathing heavily]

01:56.909 --> 01:59.036
Mr. Ga! Are you okay?

01:59.119 --> 02:00.371
Oh! Mr. Ga!

02:01.121 --> 02:03.332
Mr. Ga! Mr. Ga!

02:03.415 --> 02:04.708
Eh? [grunts]

02:06.293 --> 02:07.711
[sniffs]

02:07.795 --> 02:09.505
[grunts, stammers] What's that?

02:10.589 --> 02:11.715
Is that bird poop?

02:11.799 --> 02:13.092
[bird coos]

02:13.175 --> 02:15.052
Ugh, that's gross.

02:15.135 --> 02:16.303
[sighs, sniffs]

02:17.930 --> 02:19.098
Ew.

02:22.226 --> 02:23.644
[groans]

02:26.188 --> 02:28.440
[groaning]

02:28.524 --> 02:29.817
Mr. Ga?

02:29.900 --> 02:31.277
Mr. Ga!

02:31.360 --> 02:32.361
Mr. Ga!

02:32.444 --> 02:35.406
-Huh? Mr. Ga! Hmm?
-[bird cooing]

02:36.407 --> 02:38.576
Oh. Mr. Ga, you got to wake up!

02:39.159 --> 02:42.162
[exclaiming, panting]

02:43.163 --> 02:46.375
[breathing shakily] Mr. Ga!
Mr. Ga, wake up please!

02:46.458 --> 02:47.459
Oh, dear.

02:50.087 --> 02:51.171
Mr. Ga!

02:52.506 --> 02:55.843
Oh, no, he's not breathing! [whimpering]

02:55.926 --> 02:56.927
What do I do?

02:57.011 --> 02:58.095
[breathes heavily]

02:58.178 --> 02:59.179
Ah!

03:02.933 --> 03:05.227
[whimpers]

03:06.186 --> 03:07.479
[groans]

03:07.980 --> 03:09.106
Do it, Eui-ju.

03:09.189 --> 03:12.234
This is… this is about saving his life!

03:14.403 --> 03:15.696
[inhales deeply]

03:16.196 --> 03:17.656
-[Woo-su gasps loudly]
-[Eui-ju exclaims]

03:17.740 --> 03:19.617
[panting]

03:20.200 --> 03:22.119
Oh! Mr. Ga?

03:22.828 --> 03:24.580
Oh! Mr. Ga.

03:25.164 --> 03:26.707
Mr. Ga, are you okay?

03:26.790 --> 03:27.917
Mr. Ga.

03:28.500 --> 03:30.252
[sighs] Are you okay?

03:32.212 --> 03:34.089
It's me, Mr. Ga. I'm Yeo Eui-ju.

03:34.757 --> 03:35.758
Are you okay?

03:46.101 --> 03:47.394
What are you doing here?

03:49.480 --> 03:51.273
What am I doing here?

03:51.357 --> 03:54.693
Well, that's a bit hurtful.
I was just trying to help you.

03:54.777 --> 03:57.780
Anyway, why did you pass out here?

03:57.863 --> 04:01.033
Don't tell me it was
just because of that pigeon poop.

04:04.078 --> 04:06.497
You're kidding.
Pigeon feces have all kinds of diseases,

04:06.580 --> 04:08.415
and contain enough ammonia and uric acid

04:08.499 --> 04:10.042
to destroy a concrete bridge.

04:10.751 --> 04:11.752
Okay?

04:16.298 --> 04:17.633
Are you looking for something?

04:18.968 --> 04:20.052
Oh, your glasses.

04:20.928 --> 04:22.096
Would you like some help?

04:23.555 --> 04:25.933
-Yes.
-All right.

04:40.114 --> 04:41.240
[sighs]

04:45.077 --> 04:46.078
[glass shatters]

04:51.417 --> 04:53.419
-[gasps]
-I heard something just now.

04:53.502 --> 04:54.837
Did you just step on my glasses?

04:56.171 --> 04:57.798
[chuckles] No, not at all.

04:57.881 --> 05:00.134
It's not your glasses. [chuckles]

05:00.217 --> 05:01.844
No way. [chuckles]

05:01.927 --> 05:03.470
I… [stammers]

05:03.554 --> 05:07.099
I just stepped on a branch. [chuckles]

05:08.392 --> 05:10.019
-It snapped just like that.
-What time is it?

05:10.102 --> 05:11.854
-What?
-I asked for the time.

05:12.354 --> 05:15.024
Oh… Oh. [chuckles]

05:16.942 --> 05:18.527
It's 7:40 a.m.

05:19.987 --> 05:21.572
Go ahead and call Yoon Dong-ju.

05:24.283 --> 05:26.285
Okay. [sniffs]

05:27.870 --> 05:29.329
Mr. Ga, it's locked.

05:29.830 --> 05:31.749
-[phone face ID clicks]
-Uh, there.

05:32.416 --> 05:34.668
-Um, here you go.
-[line ringing]

05:34.752 --> 05:36.628
Is your vision really that bad?

05:37.838 --> 05:38.964
Hey. It's me.

05:39.965 --> 05:42.885
Can you grab my spare glasses
from the desk in my room?

05:42.968 --> 05:44.344
Think you can bring them to me?

05:45.179 --> 05:47.347
Yeah.
I'll wait on the road to the bus stop.

05:48.390 --> 05:49.391
Okay.

05:51.060 --> 05:53.103
[groans] Where are they?

05:56.940 --> 05:57.941
[Woo-su sighs]

05:58.025 --> 06:01.653
I told you to carpool with us.
And now look at what you've done.

06:01.737 --> 06:04.281
[Eui-ju] Oh! What do I do?

06:04.364 --> 06:06.116
Should I just throw them somewhere?

06:10.329 --> 06:11.497
[Gi-jeon] Look, a quarter.

06:12.498 --> 06:13.957
[Eui-ju] Ugh, seriously?

06:15.125 --> 06:16.168
We're running late. Let's go.

06:16.794 --> 06:19.713
Right. If we haven't found them,
they're probably gone.

06:20.589 --> 06:23.926
The way I see it,
someone who knows about glasses took them.

06:24.009 --> 06:25.886
They could tell they were expensive
right away.

06:25.969 --> 06:27.513
-Don't you think?
-Uh-huh.

06:27.596 --> 06:28.639
-Yep. Yeah.
-Right?

06:29.431 --> 06:30.766
[grunts]

06:30.849 --> 06:33.102
-I'll see you at school.
-[Eui-ju stammers]

06:40.484 --> 06:41.485
What's with that look?

06:43.612 --> 06:45.614
[blinkers clicking]

06:49.034 --> 06:50.160
Does she want a ride?

07:03.048 --> 07:04.341
[sighs]

07:05.634 --> 07:06.635
We're almost there now.

07:07.594 --> 07:09.596
Oh no. No, I'm good.

07:09.680 --> 07:11.515
I'm just really grateful for the ride.

07:20.440 --> 07:22.568
THIS IS CRAZY!

07:23.318 --> 07:25.112
Guess what?
I'm carpooling with the teachers.

07:25.195 --> 07:26.238
The PE teacher's driving,

07:26.321 --> 07:28.407
and I'm between the Japanese
and Korean lit teachers.

07:28.490 --> 07:29.491
No way!

07:31.910 --> 07:33.078
[phone buzzes]

07:33.745 --> 07:34.913
[Go-ya] How did that happen?

07:36.832 --> 07:38.709
[Eui-ju] It just did. I'll tell you later.

07:42.629 --> 07:43.839
I'm sliding back.

07:45.966 --> 07:47.009
[Dong-ju groans]

07:48.051 --> 07:49.052
Okay.

07:52.598 --> 07:54.099
[Eui-ju] I knew it.

07:54.183 --> 07:58.353
Mr. Yoon is just having to put up
with Math's selfish personality.

08:01.481 --> 08:02.482
Up all night again?

08:06.069 --> 08:08.030
It's because you didn't
let him sleep last night.

08:08.113 --> 08:11.867
-Don't you know he's a sleepyhead?
-It wasn't intentional, okay?

08:12.451 --> 08:15.204
He wanted another round.
That's what happened.

08:15.829 --> 08:17.456
I get how much you like it,

08:17.539 --> 08:19.208
but you need to let him sleep.

08:19.291 --> 08:20.292
All right?

08:21.668 --> 08:22.669
[Eui-ju] This is insane.

08:22.753 --> 08:25.130
What did they even do together all night?

08:25.214 --> 08:27.341
Dear God, please forgive me.

08:27.424 --> 08:30.469
I'll use these lines for my novel
and accept my ticket to hell.

08:32.012 --> 08:33.013
[clears throat]

08:36.391 --> 08:37.392
[Da-ju] What's wrong?

08:38.310 --> 08:40.562
Is it hot? Do you need the AC?

08:41.146 --> 08:42.147
Oh, no!

08:42.898 --> 08:44.900
No. No. [chuckling]

08:49.905 --> 08:51.990
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL

08:57.079 --> 08:59.289
[student] What gives you the right
to carpool with the teachers?

08:59.373 --> 09:01.583
[student 2] Are you mute?
Why won't you answer us?

09:01.667 --> 09:04.503
-[students clamoring]
-Come on. Say something!

09:07.589 --> 09:08.715
[Da-ju] What's she doing?

09:10.342 --> 09:12.261
[stutters] Hold on a second.
If those girls find out

09:12.344 --> 09:14.513
that I'm here with you,
they might kill me if I get off with you.

09:14.596 --> 09:18.433
[students shrieking]

09:19.059 --> 09:21.270
Oh. Oh. Oh, dear.

09:21.353 --> 09:22.980
This is not good at all. No, no, no.

09:23.063 --> 09:25.148
If they find me in this car,
they will kill me for sure.

09:25.232 --> 09:26.441
What am I supposed to do?

09:27.025 --> 09:28.610
What am I… [whimpers]

09:29.611 --> 09:30.612
Oh, oh!

09:31.113 --> 09:33.699
[students shrieking]

10:31.548 --> 10:32.674
[exhales deeply]

10:33.550 --> 10:35.761
[groans] I need more oxygen.

10:35.844 --> 10:37.929
[panting]

10:41.808 --> 10:43.268
[clears throat, clicks tongue]

10:44.102 --> 10:46.772
Well, it was a little offensive.

10:46.855 --> 10:49.149
[clears throat]
But he pulled me out of a jam.

10:54.404 --> 10:57.699
It's because
you didn't let me sleep last night.

10:58.200 --> 11:00.035
You know that I'm a sleepyhead.

11:00.535 --> 11:02.537
[chuckles]

11:02.621 --> 11:04.873
I knew it. There's definitely
something between them.

11:15.550 --> 11:16.593
Well then?

11:21.264 --> 11:22.265
Hey.

11:23.100 --> 11:24.101
Yes?

11:25.977 --> 11:27.020
Be honest now.

11:28.230 --> 11:29.231
About what?

11:30.107 --> 11:32.109
The fact that you stepped on my glasses

11:32.776 --> 11:34.444
while you were looking around for them.

11:36.071 --> 11:37.072
No, I didn't.

11:39.491 --> 11:42.160
You better not be lying
or you'll certainly regret this later.

11:42.744 --> 11:44.871
I'm definitely not lying.

11:45.872 --> 11:47.958
-And your paper?
-I'm working on it.

11:55.715 --> 11:56.716
CHAPTER 9:
HI! I'M JENNY

11:56.800 --> 11:58.260
[student] Hey, you wanna come
to my house after?

11:58.343 --> 12:01.847
Come on! Oh, oh, he's here. Hello!

12:03.723 --> 12:06.226
-Come in.
-[student gasps] What's going on?

12:06.810 --> 12:08.854
-[students chattering]
-Oh! [gasps]

12:08.937 --> 12:11.273
-Who's that?
-Oh, she's so pretty.

12:12.983 --> 12:15.193
Everyone,
this is our new exchange student,

12:15.277 --> 12:17.446
she'll be studying with you
for one semester.

12:17.988 --> 12:19.406
Introduce yourself.

12:20.866 --> 12:23.118
Hi! I'm Jenny.

12:23.201 --> 12:26.705
Uh, I am here on an exchange program
from Singapore.

12:26.788 --> 12:28.457
It's nice to meet you all.

12:28.540 --> 12:30.792
I'm really, really excited to be here.

12:30.876 --> 12:33.462
So I hope we enjoy
some great moments together.

12:34.212 --> 12:36.923
-[students cheering]
-Welcome, Jenny!

12:38.508 --> 12:40.260
-Sit over there.
-Okay.

12:42.345 --> 12:44.890
-Oh. Hi.
-Hi.

12:44.973 --> 12:47.476
-Hello.
-She's so pretty.

12:47.559 --> 12:49.144
[student chuckles]

12:50.562 --> 12:51.605
Hi!

12:56.943 --> 12:59.529
She's probably not used to
the Korean culture and school-life,

12:59.613 --> 13:00.864
so look out for her.

13:00.947 --> 13:02.073
[students] Yes, Mr. Ga.

13:02.157 --> 13:03.158
Dismissed.

13:03.783 --> 13:06.119
[students] Thank you.

13:07.454 --> 13:09.080
[Go-ya] Look, its Jenny.

13:09.164 --> 13:10.373
-[Yeong-jae] Hello!
-[Dan-ji] Hi!

13:10.457 --> 13:11.833
Hi! [chuckling]

13:11.917 --> 13:13.835
-Hi!
-Nice too meet you.

13:13.919 --> 13:15.754
My name is Yeo Eui-ju.

13:15.837 --> 13:17.547
So, uh… Oh! Are you good at Korean?

13:18.673 --> 13:19.758
Yes.

13:19.841 --> 13:20.926
Okay, we'll be like…

13:21.551 --> 13:23.303
[sighs] I'm not so good at English.

13:23.386 --> 13:25.472
Still, I'm learning, Eui-ju.

13:25.555 --> 13:27.849
Eui-ju,
I'll be able to learn fast if you help me.

13:27.933 --> 13:28.975
Ooh, good.

13:29.059 --> 13:32.187
Oh. My name is Go-ya. Nice to meet you.

13:32.270 --> 13:35.482
-Nice to meet you.
-[all laughing]

13:36.107 --> 13:39.986
Jenny, uh, why did you come to Korea?

13:40.529 --> 13:42.906
Uh… Doesn't everybody
want to come to Korea?

13:42.989 --> 13:44.032
[Yeong-jae] Uh…

13:44.115 --> 13:45.784
There's a lot of delicious food.

13:45.867 --> 13:49.746
And I'd love to visit all the locations
from Korean dramas.

13:49.829 --> 13:51.331
-[Yeong-jae] Right.
-Right, the dramas.

13:51.414 --> 13:52.916
Yeah, that's right.

13:53.416 --> 13:58.129
So then, uh why did you come to Jeonju
and not Seoul?

13:58.838 --> 14:02.551
Well, of course, I did apply
to go to a school in Seoul at first.

14:02.634 --> 14:06.137
But… I was on the computer,
and I was like… [imitates clicking mouse]

14:07.430 --> 14:09.766
Eh? And chose this school by mistake.

14:09.849 --> 14:11.685
-[all mumbling]
-[Yeong-jae] By mistake.

14:11.768 --> 14:13.520
-By mistake, yeah, of course.
-[clamoring]

14:13.603 --> 14:15.605
-You selected the wrong one.
-Yes, but it's okay.

14:15.689 --> 14:18.400
But it's okay. This place is great, like…

14:18.483 --> 14:19.901
Jeonju is beautiful.

14:19.985 --> 14:22.279
-[Eui-ju] That's right. yeah!
-Yep, Jeonju is really pretty.

14:22.362 --> 14:26.157
CHAPTER 10:
I'M GOING TO TUMBLE YOU AROUND

14:28.577 --> 14:29.578
[sighs]

14:31.329 --> 14:32.330
[sniffs]

14:33.290 --> 14:34.874
Oh. [sighs]

14:34.958 --> 14:37.627
Is it because
he was wearing different glasses?

14:38.628 --> 14:40.338
He looked like he didn't feel well.

14:42.173 --> 14:44.676
Oh, oh, oh… Ah…

14:45.927 --> 14:47.220
[sighs]

14:47.762 --> 14:50.974
Ugh! Why won't this work?

14:52.225 --> 14:54.269
[groans] Shouldn't I just throw them away?

14:54.853 --> 14:57.397
[clicks tongue] No, I shouldn't.

14:57.981 --> 15:00.400
I should give them back to him. [sniffs]

15:00.483 --> 15:02.944
The spare ones weren't his prescription.

15:03.528 --> 15:07.449
[sighs] C-come on. We can do this!

15:07.532 --> 15:09.451
[Da-ju] Type one verbs

15:09.534 --> 15:12.454
are basically most verbs
that don't end "ru".

15:12.537 --> 15:14.998
For example, "ikuro" becomes "ikanai"

15:15.081 --> 15:18.668
because ku of the a-row version is ka.

15:18.752 --> 15:21.129
Now, type two verbs are easier.

15:21.212 --> 15:22.505
You simply drop the ru.

15:24.299 --> 15:27.135
So, then it becomes tabenai.

15:28.511 --> 15:29.804
Type three verbs…

15:35.018 --> 15:39.064
I'M TRULY SORRY

15:46.613 --> 15:48.198
JAPANESE LANGUAGE

15:52.702 --> 15:55.455
Right in the middle of my class.

15:57.832 --> 16:00.251
You aren't even paying attention to me.

16:01.711 --> 16:03.713
I can't believe this.

16:09.135 --> 16:10.136
[sighs]

16:15.809 --> 16:16.935
How are you feeling?

16:17.435 --> 16:20.313
I feel like I'm stuck watching
a super-fast Mandelbrot

16:21.064 --> 16:22.941
zoom around and it won't stop.

16:23.942 --> 16:25.193
A Man… what?

16:26.778 --> 16:27.779
I feel dizzy.

16:29.698 --> 16:31.866
Oh, okay.

16:37.831 --> 16:38.915
Come in.

16:43.753 --> 16:45.130
[sighs]

16:47.590 --> 16:49.175
Mr. Ga, your student

16:49.259 --> 16:53.221
got caught doing your homework
during my Japanese class.

16:54.389 --> 16:56.975
She is all yours now. [scoffs]

17:05.233 --> 17:07.235
-Read it now.
-Excuse me?

17:09.195 --> 17:11.448
Uh, will you just read it quietly alone?

17:11.948 --> 17:13.658
There are other teachers here.

17:24.294 --> 17:25.420
"Dear Mr. Euclid."

17:26.171 --> 17:27.213
I can't hear you.

17:29.716 --> 17:30.717
"Greetings.

17:33.636 --> 17:39.142
My name… is Yeo Eui-ju
and I am 18-year-old girl

17:39.225 --> 17:43.146
from Jeonju in the year 2026.

17:46.649 --> 17:49.944
Back in seventh grade,
I faced public embarrassment

17:50.028 --> 17:53.740
because of a math proofs question
during my math class.

17:53.823 --> 17:56.242
The trauma from that day

17:56.326 --> 17:59.329
led me to give up on math entirely.

17:59.412 --> 18:03.333
Why were you so obsessed
with those things, sir?

18:03.416 --> 18:05.960
Is something truly useless
if it cannot be proven?

18:06.669 --> 18:08.713
I wonder had I been born before you,

18:08.797 --> 18:10.799
would I have been spared
such persecution?"

18:14.385 --> 18:16.554
It's a reflection not a protest letter.

18:20.141 --> 18:21.142
"However,

18:21.226 --> 18:25.480
the opening line of your book,
'A point is that which has no part,'

18:25.563 --> 18:29.567
struck me with…
struck me with true admiration, sir.

18:30.527 --> 18:33.905
Even a math hater like me
could understand it right away.

18:35.031 --> 18:36.282
Therefore,

18:36.366 --> 18:40.119
I am awfully sorry
that my ignorance disappointed you

18:40.203 --> 18:43.665
and I deeply regret
my lack of understanding in math."

18:44.707 --> 18:46.251
That's all I wrote so far.

18:47.001 --> 18:49.629
Two demerit points
for writing it during class.

18:49.712 --> 18:52.340
-[groans]
-What? Is it unfair?

18:53.925 --> 18:55.051
No, sir.

18:56.761 --> 18:58.930
Looking out for a friend
and showing empathy

18:59.013 --> 19:01.474
are among the most essential lessons
a school should provide.

19:04.727 --> 19:06.312
You'll look out for Ji-a as of today.

19:06.396 --> 19:09.190
If she's late or absent
or if she ditches class or an assembly

19:09.274 --> 19:10.525
she'll get two demerit points,

19:10.608 --> 19:11.734
while you'll get…

19:11.818 --> 19:13.361
four points.

19:15.405 --> 19:16.573
-What?
-Dismissed.

19:18.032 --> 19:20.034
-You can't do that!
-[sighs]

19:20.118 --> 19:21.119
Mr. Ga!

19:23.746 --> 19:25.290
That's unfair.

19:25.373 --> 19:26.541
Please, Mr. Ga…

19:29.377 --> 19:30.837
Geez. [whimpers]

19:31.838 --> 19:32.964
[exhales deeply]

19:33.882 --> 19:35.758
[Go-ya] Dang, that's actually ridiculous.

19:35.842 --> 19:38.678
He can't give you more demerit points
than Choi Ji-a.

19:38.761 --> 19:41.347
Why is he always on Eui-ju's case, though?

19:41.431 --> 19:42.765
Is he just being a hater?

19:42.849 --> 19:44.684
Or maybe…

19:44.767 --> 19:48.021
-he's into her. [laughs]
-[Dan-ji laughs]

19:48.104 --> 19:50.565
Could it be that you remind him
of his ex-girlfriend?

19:50.648 --> 19:52.859
Maybe he wants to give Eui-ju a hard time

19:52.942 --> 19:55.194
-because she reminds him of being dumped.
-Nah.

19:55.278 --> 19:58.865
What if your parents and Mr. Ga's parents
are enemies or something?

19:58.948 --> 20:00.700
Huh? Could be. [laughing]

20:00.783 --> 20:02.660
-[Dan-ji, Go-ya laugh]
-Girls,

20:03.411 --> 20:04.454
-knock it off.
-Or maybe…

20:04.537 --> 20:06.998
he's just unhappy with how you look.

20:07.582 --> 20:09.042
-That may be it!
-[laughing]

20:09.125 --> 20:10.168
Hey!

20:12.128 --> 20:13.588
Let's try this.

20:16.132 --> 20:17.926
[students] Hello Mr. Ga.

20:19.302 --> 20:20.511
Where did we leave off?

20:21.679 --> 20:22.722
[Go-ya] Mr. Ga,

20:23.473 --> 20:25.224
Eui-ju is feeling a little sick.

20:26.976 --> 20:27.977
How sick are you?

20:29.270 --> 20:30.605
[Eui-ju groaning]

20:30.688 --> 20:33.149
Ow, I don't know, Mr. Ga.

20:33.232 --> 20:36.402
My head is spinning
and I feel so nauseous.

20:36.486 --> 20:39.489
Oh, my goodness. Oh, dear.

20:40.615 --> 20:42.241
I don't know what to do.

20:42.742 --> 20:45.495
I can't stand this. [panting]

20:45.578 --> 20:47.538
I literally feel like dying.

20:48.581 --> 20:49.582
[sighs]

20:50.166 --> 20:51.417
[groans]

20:58.257 --> 20:59.258
Yeo Eui-ju.

21:00.635 --> 21:01.719
Yes?

21:02.762 --> 21:05.264
Explain the definition
of the right and left hand limit.

21:06.057 --> 21:07.058
[groans]

21:21.948 --> 21:25.994
Even if both the left and right-hand
limits exist, without equal values,

21:26.077 --> 21:28.621
-does the limit exist?
-Huh?

21:28.705 --> 21:30.289
If a point's detached from the graph

21:30.373 --> 21:31.666
what kind of discontinuity is it?

21:32.291 --> 21:33.292
[stammers]

21:33.835 --> 21:37.130
Which conditions prove that f(x)
is continuous at x equals a?

21:38.548 --> 21:40.008
[sighs]

21:41.175 --> 21:43.636
We went over this during the last class,
did we not?

21:44.470 --> 21:46.389
If you'd studied
instead of faking illness,

21:46.472 --> 21:47.807
you would've known.

21:51.352 --> 21:52.520
[Woo-su] What are you doing here?

21:56.024 --> 21:58.067
You ready to take
the Discrete Math lecture?

21:58.151 --> 21:59.861
[Eui-ju] And cut!

22:02.030 --> 22:04.032
[sighs, clicks tongue]

22:06.826 --> 22:08.119
Ju Si-on!

22:09.454 --> 22:12.165
-Yes?
-I already mentioned this last time.

22:12.248 --> 22:13.750
Weren't you paying attention?

22:14.375 --> 22:15.752
The rest of you did a good job.

22:16.586 --> 22:18.129
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

22:18.212 --> 22:21.591
So, you can't read between the lines?
Is that it?

22:23.092 --> 22:25.887
In this scene, you're supposed
to feel jealous and angry

22:25.970 --> 22:28.264
at the sight of Yoon and Tae-ha
talking together.

22:28.347 --> 22:30.725
So, your lines
should give a sense of superiority,

22:30.808 --> 22:34.187
like, "Yoon already decided to follow me

22:34.270 --> 22:36.272
but you're far below my match."

22:36.355 --> 22:37.356
Don't you get it?

22:38.566 --> 22:39.567
That's just what I did.

22:40.401 --> 22:41.527
[scoffs]

22:43.029 --> 22:44.822
How dare you talk back to me?

22:48.159 --> 22:49.660
I'm a writer.

22:50.203 --> 22:52.789
And you're just a character in my novel.

22:52.872 --> 22:54.540
Get it? I'm a writer…

22:57.919 --> 22:59.128
I mean…

23:00.171 --> 23:02.757
You're a character in my novel.

23:02.840 --> 23:06.969
Listen, why must you
always have it your way? Huh?

23:07.053 --> 23:08.763
Everything has meaning.

23:08.846 --> 23:12.433
Even a single punctuation mark
in my lines matters!

23:12.517 --> 23:16.729
Now stop complaining
and just do as I say, okay?

23:16.813 --> 23:18.272
Yes. Of course, ma'am.

23:19.398 --> 23:20.858
[Woo-su] What are you huffing about?

23:27.615 --> 23:31.536
The basic concepts of functions,
write them, ten times each.

23:32.537 --> 23:33.704
Yes, sir.

23:38.835 --> 23:41.087
[Eui-ju] Regretful Ju Si-on.

23:41.170 --> 23:42.171
Wait and see.

23:42.255 --> 23:46.008
I'm going to tumble you around
until you can't tell which way is up.

23:46.092 --> 23:47.510
You'll literally be rolling.

23:47.593 --> 23:49.178
CHAPTER 11:
HE NEVER LIKED ME TO BEGIN WITH

23:49.262 --> 23:51.389
-These are mini meat patties.
-Delicious. Mmm.

23:51.472 --> 23:52.473
Is this pork?

23:52.557 --> 23:54.517
-[Go-ya] No. It's a fish cutlet.
-[Dan-ji] Hey, Jenny.

23:54.600 --> 23:55.685
Do you like the food okay?

23:56.185 --> 23:57.895
-It's delicious.
-Delicious, right?

23:57.979 --> 24:00.773
-Mm-hmm.
-Don't get into it, or you'll gain weight.

24:02.358 --> 24:04.402
-[Dan-ji] Eat up. It's all right.
-Uh, Jenny.

24:04.986 --> 24:06.112
Do you have a boyfriend?

24:06.195 --> 24:07.530
Mm-hmm.

24:08.114 --> 24:09.157
[gasps]

24:10.283 --> 24:11.284
He's from Brazil.

24:11.367 --> 24:12.952
-Brazil?
-[Dan-ji] Whoa.

24:13.035 --> 24:14.829
His name is Luiz.

24:14.912 --> 24:17.081
-You're totally global, huh?
-[all chuckling]

24:17.165 --> 24:18.708
So how did you guys meet?

24:18.791 --> 24:20.626
Hmm, we met at the Louvre in Paris.

24:20.710 --> 24:22.253
He's in college studying photography.

24:22.336 --> 24:24.672
He kept asking me to be his model.

24:24.755 --> 24:27.175
So, we got together from then on.

24:28.509 --> 24:30.261
Then, is he in France now?

24:30.344 --> 24:31.387
Uh-huh.

24:32.096 --> 24:34.140
-I bet you miss him.
-Mm-hmm.

24:34.724 --> 24:37.018
I do. And he also says that without me,

24:37.101 --> 24:38.352
food only tastes half as good

24:39.103 --> 24:41.314
and that he smiles half as often.

24:41.397 --> 24:43.149
[chuckles] Isn't that hilarious?

24:43.232 --> 24:44.901
Men from South America are different.

24:44.984 --> 24:46.319
What do you know?

24:46.402 --> 24:49.030
I know enough. [grunts]

24:49.113 --> 24:51.282
Jenny, what did your boyfriend say

24:51.365 --> 24:53.492
when he asked you
to be his model at the Louvre?

24:55.036 --> 24:56.621
"Excuse me, miss.

24:56.704 --> 24:59.916
I spent all day
chasing the perfect sunset,

25:00.499 --> 25:04.545
only to find something
far more beautiful right here.

25:05.213 --> 25:08.841
Would it be okay with you
if I captured this moment?"

25:09.342 --> 25:10.593
Wow.

25:11.302 --> 25:12.929
How romantic.

25:13.012 --> 25:14.597
[laughing]

25:17.516 --> 25:21.938
YUL EYE CLINIC

25:22.521 --> 25:25.024
PRESCRIPTION

25:39.372 --> 25:44.085
BUBU PHARMACY

25:45.336 --> 25:47.880
Okay, your medication for seven days.

25:47.964 --> 25:49.840
Make sure to take it after every meal.

25:49.924 --> 25:52.426
This is the anti-inflammatory
and this is for your stomach.

25:52.510 --> 25:54.679
-All right.
-And also,

25:54.762 --> 25:55.972
these are the steroid eye drops,

25:56.055 --> 25:58.808
so make sure you shake them good
before you put them in.

25:58.891 --> 26:00.142
That will be 6.37, please.

26:02.478 --> 26:04.480
Your eyes are so bloodshot.

26:05.314 --> 26:07.984
Your glasses tell me
that you haven't had LASIK.

26:08.067 --> 26:09.527
You should get new glasses soon.

26:09.610 --> 26:11.279
Eyes are very important, you know?

26:14.073 --> 26:16.075
[soulful music playing]

26:38.764 --> 26:40.099
[music stops abruptly]

26:40.182 --> 26:41.934
Ah. [laughing]

26:43.227 --> 26:44.729
Geez, I'm sorry.

26:45.479 --> 26:48.983
It was totally like a scene
from a comic book just now.

26:49.066 --> 26:50.860
You know, when they take off their glasses

26:50.943 --> 26:55.239
and poof, they just transform
into a total hottie. [laughs]

26:59.201 --> 27:01.662
You should really try
getting contact lenses.

27:05.416 --> 27:06.417
Goodbye.

27:12.006 --> 27:13.007
Anime-level.

27:14.884 --> 27:16.010
Anime-level.

27:22.892 --> 27:24.518
AFTER-SCHOOL PROGRAM APPLICATION

27:24.602 --> 27:26.771
Bring it back
with your parents' signature.

27:26.854 --> 27:27.855
Yes, sir.

27:38.199 --> 27:40.326
What the… Is he sick or something?

27:42.411 --> 27:43.662
What did the doctor say?

27:45.331 --> 27:48.250
It takes at least two weeks
to make new glasses.

27:48.334 --> 27:49.335
Two weeks?

27:49.877 --> 27:51.504
How are you going to hang in there?

27:55.758 --> 27:56.759
Good job.

27:56.842 --> 27:58.677
[students] Thank you.

27:58.761 --> 28:00.763
[chattering, laughing]

28:05.684 --> 28:06.685
Hey!

28:07.269 --> 28:08.270
Ji-a!

28:08.354 --> 28:10.523
Hey, Ji-a! Where are you going?

28:10.606 --> 28:11.732
You need stay.

28:13.442 --> 28:14.610
You're off to work, right?

28:15.194 --> 28:16.779
Um, can't you leave after the bell?

28:16.862 --> 28:19.698
I get demerit points when you're not
at the school or assemblies.

28:21.450 --> 28:22.910
Hey!

28:22.993 --> 28:25.371
[groans]
Can't you just do me this one favor?

28:26.205 --> 28:27.415
[sighs]

28:27.498 --> 28:28.916
I'm forced to do this too.

28:29.959 --> 28:30.960
[sighs]

28:36.215 --> 28:37.633
Mr. Ga! You saw that just now, right?

28:37.716 --> 28:39.718
I did tell her
to stay until the dismissal,

28:39.802 --> 28:42.388
but she just ignored me
and left without hesitation.

28:46.642 --> 28:50.646
Uh, could you…
could you maybe not count this one then?

28:50.729 --> 28:52.940
You know
there's nothing I can do about it.

28:56.110 --> 28:57.361
Yeo Eui-ju.

28:58.863 --> 29:00.739
-Four demerit points.
-[book slams shut]

29:09.165 --> 29:12.710
GENERAL WASTE

29:13.294 --> 29:14.462
[sighs]

29:14.545 --> 29:16.255
Go-ya was right.

29:16.338 --> 29:18.048
It went wrong from the very start.

29:18.632 --> 29:20.759
He simply never liked me at all.

29:23.554 --> 29:24.805
[grunts]

29:25.848 --> 29:28.100
I saw you filming us. Delete it.

29:28.184 --> 29:30.811
You will write a letter to Euclid.
Twenty pages.

29:30.895 --> 29:32.438
[clicks tongue]

29:32.521 --> 29:33.522
Yeo Eui-ju.

29:34.148 --> 29:35.524
Four demerit points.

29:36.567 --> 29:38.777
[upbeat rock music playing]

30:55.563 --> 30:56.564
[music ends]
